<section class="methodology">
  <div class="methodology-inner">
    <p class="section-label">The Methodology</p>
    <h2 class="section-title" style="color: var(--ivory);">How the Throughput Diagnostic Works</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">
      Based on Eli Goldratt's Theory of Constraints — the same framework used by manufacturing leaders worldwide. Applied to AI implementation, it ensures every dollar you spend on AI targets the ONE thing holding your business back.
    </p>

    <div class="steps-grid">
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-number">01</span>
        <h3 class="step-title">Map the System</h3>
        <p class="step-desc">Walk through your entire business end-to-end. Not your tech stack — your value stream. From customer discovery to payment and retention.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step-arrow">&rarr;</div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-number">02</span>
        <h3 class="step-title">Find the Constraint</h3>
        <p class="step-desc">Where does work pile up? Where do customers wait? What's the ONE thing that, if it ran twice as fast, would make everything faster?</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step-arrow">&rarr;</div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-number">03</span>
        <h3 class="step-title">Prescribe the AI</h3>
        <p class="step-desc">Match the constraint to the right solution. Not enough leads? Prong 1. Operations bottleneck? Prong 2. Team overwhelmed? Prong 3.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step-arrow">&rarr;</div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-number">04</span>
        <h3 class="step-title">Deliver the Roadmap</h3>
        <p class="step-desc">A branded report with the constraint identified, specific AI solution, expected ROI with math you can follow, and what NOT to automate yet.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

